meta {
  name: Complete
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseURL}}/google-calendar/complete/
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {"code": "{{google_oauth_code}}"}
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
}

docs {
  Finishes the connection using the `code` the frontend received from the
  `/callback/` redirect. Exchanges the code with Google, fetches the
  connected account's own email, and requires it to exactly match
  settings.GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID (the one fixed shared organizer account) - 400
  "This is not the shared Google Calendar account..." otherwise. Only then
  does it save the tokens onto whichever User's login email
  (User.email) matches that address and who has an active Admin or
  Associate profile - not necessarily the signed-in caller. 400 "No
  active Biopeak admin or staff account uses this Google account's
  email..." if no matching active login - the shared account's own
  login email must equal GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID.

  Set env var google_oauth_code to the `code` value from the URL fragment
  (after the `#`) your browser lands on after approving consent (see
  Connect.bru's docs for the full manual flow) - paste it there, not
  directly into this body, so this request stays runnable straight from the
  collection.

  Method: POST
  Path: /google-calendar/complete/
  Source: integrations.google_calendar.views.GoogleCalendarCompleteView
  Auth: None — authentication_classes = [] (this view never reads
  request.user; the email match is what decides whose tokens actually get
  saved). Collection may attach Bearer if logged in; view ignores it.

  Success: {"detail": "Google Calendar connected.", "data": {"google_email": "...", "user_id": "..."}}
}
